{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'arbitration|BLOCK|shadow|constant|forg|fallback|deviation' collab/1793309600000-architect-yang-call-kimi-r4-arbitration.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log\"","aggregated_output":"7:  ## (a) Hand-constructed-descriptor contradiction — source forgery is nonconformant\n15:  **Ruling:** the current source-level `assoc` forgery is a conformance blocker. Do not resolve this by declaring every entry-spelled Clojure map a profile projection.\n17:  **Recommendation:** distinguish constructor/profile-produced descriptors from ordinary source maps at source resolution, without adding a VM type, descriptor seal, or provenance registry. Keep the hand-constructed fixture only as explicit UAST/profile construction. Add negative tests for entry-spelled source data, copied entries, and `assoc`-forged descriptors.\n37:  Replacing constant-depth assertions with assertions of linear growth documents a regression; it does not establish conformance. Successful deep recursion and the absence of a hard VM depth limit do not preserve tail behavior.\n39:  **Ruling:** constant-stack tail behavior remains required. This is not approved as a tradeoff with an unspecified future optimization.\n41:  **Recommendation:** restore constant-stack named and mutual tail calls in the entry/bridge design. Reinstate constant-depth assertions for both execution lanes. Any later fast path must separately prove all A2 requirements, and correctness must not depend on it.\n43:  ## (e) P3 records — continuation fallback requires fixing; named binding is conformant\n45:  **Non-callable captured continuation:** the fallback that returns `escape` as a successful value is wrong even if currently unreachable. Replace it with explicit qualified failure; a continuation must never silently become the call result.\n49:  **Final disposition:** adoption remains blocked on (a)–(d), plus the continuation fallback in (e). The named-argument condition needs no reclassification. No files were changed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
