{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793309600000-architect-yang-call-kimi-r4-arbitration.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc'","aggregated_output":"kimi version 2.4.0\n• I'll reread three now per user. I have content but explicit read. Should date fresh GMT via bash. Can parallel 3 reads date. Then deliver reordered.2026-10-30 13:42:12 GMT\nRespond exactly begins timestamp then complete. No Completed-Local asked but format likely add. Use current local not needed.\n\n• Completed-GMT: 2026-10-30 13:42:12 GMT\n\n  ## (a) Hand-constructed-descriptor contradiction — source forgery is nonconformant\n\n  The orchestrator’s fixture instruction and A1’s data-map obligation address different levels:\n\n  - A hand-constructed descriptor in **UAST** is a valid profile-level construction and may test the common invocation path.\n  - A Clojure source map constructed or modified with `assoc` remains source data. Copying `:yang.call/entry` into it must not make it callable.\n  - Structural projection is valid **after callable admission**; it is not itself proof of admission.\n\n  **Ruling:** the current source-level `assoc` forgery is a conformance blocker. Do not resolve this by declaring every entry-spelled Clojure map a profile projection.\n\n  **Recommendation:** distinguish constructor/profile-produced descriptors from ordinary source maps at source resolution, without adding a VM type, descriptor seal, or provenance registry. Keep the hand-constructed fixture only as explicit UAST/profile construction. Add negative tests for entry-spelled source data, copied entries, and `assoc`-forged descriptors.\n\n  ## (b) Shadowable-names fix — prefer hygienic `dsg__` aliases\n\n  Both proposed fixes could stop the capture, but rejecting user bindings of `get`, `=`, `assoc`, and `empty?` unnecessarily changes the Clojure source language to accommodate generated code.\n\n  **Ruling:** use compiler-private `dsg__` aliases established beside the prepended `call/uast`, and emit those aliases throughout generated entry and caller-bridge code. Local binding rejection is not the preferred fix.\n\n  **Recommendation:** test every captured name around function construction and invocation, including successful returns and exception/raise paths. Generated code must be insulated from all source lexical bindings.\n\n  ## (c) Direct-branch scope — compiler-private calls only\n\n  The prompt’s allowance for “pre-adopted program values” was broader than A2 and is superseded by A2. A source application may not use structural entry absence as permission for direct application.\n\n  **Ruling:** every source-resolved application goes through common callable admission. Missing entry means `:yang.call/not-callable`, not direct application and not a raw host/VM defect. Only explicitly compiler-generated implementation calls may remain direct.\n\n  **Recommendation:** restrict the direct branch to private generated callees rather than arbitrary entry-less runtime values. Test scalars, ordinary maps, malformed descriptors, and entry-less foreign values. Internal adapters and continuations may remain private only where their calls are genuinely compiler-generated.\n\n  ## (d) Tail-stack tradeoff — do not accept the regression\n\n  Replacing constant-depth assertions with assertions of linear growth documents a regression; it does not establish conformance. Successful deep recursion and the absence of a hard VM depth limit do not preserve tail behavior.\n\n  **Ruling:** constant-stack tail behavior remains required. This is not approved as a tradeoff with an unspecified future optimization.\n\n  **Recommendation:** restore constant-stack named and mutual tail calls in the entry/bridge design. Reinstate constant-depth assertions for both execution lanes. Any later fast path must separately prove all A2 requirements, and correctness must not depend on it.\n\n  ## (e) P3 records — continuation fallback requires fixing; named binding is conformant\n\n  **Non-callable captured continuation:** the fallback that returns `escape` as a successful value is wrong even if currently unreachable. Replace it with explicit qualified failure; a continuation must never silently become the call result.\n\n  **Nonempty named arguments:** retain `:yang.call/thrown`. Under §8.10.7, callee argument-binding failures carry the actual callee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`; `:yang.call/unsupported-binding` is for protocol/profile binding failures. The existing classification is therefore conformant, provided the complete original error payload remains intact.\n\n  **Final disposition:** adoption remains blocked on (a)–(d), plus the continuation fallback in (e). The named-argument condition needs no reclassification. No files were changed.\n\nTo resume this session: kimi -r session_375e0301-61bb-4cd3-ad2d-2a4fb2adb18b\n(ns yang.core.call\n  \"Language-neutral guest calling convention (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   §8.10). This namespace emits the same pure definitions into bundled\n   preludes and the linked `yang.call` module.\"\n  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module that publishes the shared calling runtime.\"\n  'yang.call)\n\n\n(def host-names\n  \"Host module names read by the guest definitions.\"\n  '#{cell/get data/callable? data/contains? data/count data/map?\n     data/string? data/vector?})\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The one ordered definition list used by both emitters.\"\n  '[;; Descriptor projection remains structural after callable admission.\n    [yang.call/_descriptor\n     (fn [callable]\n       (if (data/map? callable)\n         (if (= (get callable :type) :cell-ref)\n           (cell/get callable)\n           callable)\n         nil))]\n    [yang.call/entry\n     (fn [callable]\n       (get (yang.call/_descriptor callable) :yang.call/entry))]\n    [yang.call/eligible?\n     (fn [callable]\n       (let [descriptor (yang.call/_descriptor callable)]\n         (if (nil? (yang.call/entry callable))\n           false\n           (if (data/contains? descriptor :yang.call/eligible?)\n             ((get descriptor :yang.call/eligible?) callable)\n             true))))]\n    [yang.call/invocation\n     (fn [callee positional named raise]\n       (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee callee)\n                            :yang.call/positional positional)\n                     :yang.call/named named)\n              :yang.call/raise raise))]\n    [yang.call/invocation-with\n     (fn [callee positional named raise options]\n       (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc options :yang.call/callee callee)\n                            :yang.call/positional positional)\n                     :yang.call/named named)\n              :yang.call/raise raise))]\n    [yang.call/_pair?\n     (fn [pair]\n       (if (data/vector? pair)\n         (= (data/count pair) 2)\n         false))]\n    [yang.call/_named-pairs?\n     (fn [pairs index]\n       (if (= index (data/count pairs))\n         true\n         (let [pair (data/nth pairs index)]\n           (if (yang.call/_pair? pair)\n             (if (data/string? (data/nth pair 0))\n               (yang.call/_named-pairs? pairs (+ index 1))\n               false)\n             false))))]\n    [yang.call/valid-invocation?\n     (fn [invocation]\n       (if (data/map? invocation)\n         (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/callee)\n           (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/positional)\n             (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/named)\n               (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/raise)\n                 (if (data/vector? (get invocation :yang.call/positional))\n                   (if (data/vector? (get invocation :yang.call/named))\n                     (yang.call/_named-pairs?\n                       (get invocation :yang.call/named) 0)\n                     false)\n                   false)\n                 false)\n               false)\n             false)\n           false)\n         false))]\n    [yang.call/condition\n     (fn [reason evidence]\n       (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/reason reason)\n              :yang.call/data evidence))]\n    [yang.call/thrown\n     (fn [value]\n       (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown)\n              :yang.call/value value))]\n    [yang.call/transfer\n     (fn [raise condition]\n       (raise condition))]\n    [yang.call/invoke\n     (fn [callable positional named raise]\n       (if (data/callable? raise)\n         (if (yang.call/eligible? callable)\n           (let [target (yang.call/entry callable)\n                 record (yang.call/invocation callable positional named raise)]\n             (if (not (nil? target))\n               (if (yang.call/valid-invocation? record)\n                 (target record)\n                 (yang.call/transfer\n                   raise\n                   (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                        {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n               (yang.call/transfer\n                 raise\n                 (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                      {:yang.call/callee callable}))))\n           (yang.call/transfer\n             raise\n             (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\n                                  {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n         (raise (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                     {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}))))]\n    [yang.call/invoke-with\n     (fn [callable positional named raise options]\n       (if (data/callable? raise)\n         (if (yang.call/eligible? callable)\n           (let [target (yang.call/entry callable)\n                 record (yang.call/invocation-with\n                          callable positional named raise options)]\n             (if (not (nil? target))\n               (if (yang.call/valid-invocation? record)\n                 (target record)\n                 (yang.call/transfer\n                   raise\n                   (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                        {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n               (yang.call/transfer\n                 raise\n                 (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                      {:yang.call/callee callable}))))\n           (yang.call/transfer\n             raise\n             (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\n                                  {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n         (raise (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                     {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}))))]])\n\n\n(def ^:private public-exports\n  '#{entry eligible? invocation invocation-with valid-invocation? condition\n     thrown transfer invoke invoke-with})\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled definitions, in source order and tail marked.\"\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (reduce (fn [ast [key form]]\n              (u/then ast (u/def! key (u/sexp->uast form))))\n            (u/def! (ffirst definitions)\n                    (u/sexp->uast (second (first definitions))))\n            (rest definitions))))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  \"The linked module tree built from the same `definitions`.\"\n  (let [stripped (core/module-definitions \"yang.call\" :yang.call/uninit\n                                          [] definitions)]\n    (core/module-tree stripped [])))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"Public module exports (private helper definitions stay internal).\"\n  public-exports)\n\n\n(def ^:private module-free-names\n  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"The linker module spec for `yang.call` over `registry`.\"\n  [registry]\n  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name\n                     :ast module-uast\n                     :exports module-exports\n                     :requires {}\n                     :free-names module-free-names\n                     :registry registry\n                     :message \"the yang.call module reads an undeclared name\"\n                     :refusal-ns \"yang.call\"}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
