{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn.*(walker-run|semantic-run)|depth' test/yang/clojure_test.clj; rg --files test/yang/latte_oracle | sort; rg -n 'deviation|Deviation' docs | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"986:;; --- continuation-depth gates -----------------------------------------------\n988:(defn- walker-depth\n995:(defn- semantic-depth\n1002:   maximum depth `depth-of` reports in :max-depth.\"\n1003:  [depth-of]\n1005:    (loop [v vm, mx (depth-of vm)]\n1007:        (assoc v :max-depth mx)\n1009:          (recur v' (max mx (depth-of v'))))))))\n1012:(defn- walker-run\n1013:  \"[value max-depth] of `ast` on the walker lane.\"\n1020:               (stepper walker-depth))]\n1021:    [(vm/value (:consumer done)) (:max-depth (:consumer done))]))\n1024:(defn- semantic-run\n1025:  \"[value max-depth] of `ast` on the semantic lane.\"\n1048:                                       load-rows (stepper semantic-depth))]\n1049:      [(vm/value (:consumer done)) (:max-depth (:consumer done))])))\n1078:(deftest test-continuation-depth-gates\n1088:      (is (= d100 d1000) (str label \": depth is constant in the iteration count\"))\n1090:        (is (<= d1000 (+ d0 2)) (str label \": at most 2 above the pre-loop depth\")))))\n1091:  ;; The walker lane masks a missing flag (its depth stays flat either way),\n1093:  (testing \"negative control: without :tail? on the self-application depth grows\"\n1355:(deftest test-outcome-common-call-depth\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/case_arms.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/context.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice7_anchors.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice8_evidence.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/slice8_sequences.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/throw_sites.edn\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/unfold_implicit.edn\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:702:- **Deviation from the plan's C2**: schema needed three regions, not two.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:768:  so the three-region schema deviation stands.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:1375:Two deviations the implementer disclosed rather than absorbed, both judged\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:2006:One deviation, disclosed rather than smuggled: three of §4.1's six new\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:2572:Verification: Findings verified locally (1138 lines, complete across all 7 sections, 10 recorded deviations with rationale). Claude CLI execution exited 0 with full stdout log preserved.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:5779:Decisions: Reviewer budget conserved by closing per its own pre-authorization instead of a third fable round (fable at ~17% until Tuesday 04:00). The codex -s-after-resume flag error recurred once and was fixed by parent-level placement (codex exec -s workspace-write resume <id>); the failed invocation is the first 178 bytes of the r3 log. R4 was delegated to the architect with the reviewer's recommendation as default and a deviation duty; no deviation occurred.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6017:Next: (a) reconcile both J1 reviews; (b) opus fix round; (c) one architect turn: rule on the decode-not-through-Boring deviation, the Node keyword collapse (class vocabulary) and README N/A table errata, then sign off J1 (Boring behavior and no existing-code change); (d) commit J1 to jing-cbor; (e) J2 (Dart codec, cbor 6.5.1) with GLM or qwen as reviewer; J3 conformance; then owner gates. Push, merge, archive collab/ (over 100 artifacts) await the owner.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:6123:Done: (1) B1's second-round review (deepseek-v4-pro, artifact 1790063000000-*): confirmed all nine round-1 findings genuinely fixed in the working tree (traced by hand, not trusted), P1-2's scope-conflict fix shown to generalize to three adversarial variants beyond the reviewed fixture (a three-declaration case, a cross-body :jump re-reach, a length-differing chain). Found two more real issues: a CLJD `String/fromCharCode` slash-vs-dot named-constructor syntax error in the round-1 fix's own new test fixture (would