ould be invoked with raw args (silent wrong on arity collision); no HOF primitive exists today; the corpus's one first-class use is (partial free-vars def-env); architect note: ledger now, closes when slice 5/7 apply/partial land | slice 3b review (glm session 79d4df98) | yang.clojure | slice 7 | P3 |\n| yang.clojure: three slice-4 residuals, bundled per architect disposition (fable 1793212600000): (1) a free REFERENCE to a reserved-prefix worker name (dsg__loop0 etc.) is not refused — binder enforcement covers bindings only, so user-typed (dsg__loop0 dsg__loop0 3) inside a 2-binding loop reaches the worker and nil-fills; closing route: a compile-program pre-pass refusing reserved-prefix symbols in any position; (2) bare recur/loop symbols in VALUE position compile as ordinary variables (host Clojure rejects unbound recur; binder-shadowed case matches Clojure); closing route: same pre-pass refusing recur/loop outside operator position; (3) the wrong-operand-count rejection message says \"loop bindings\" also for function-level targets (cosmetic; target records its kind) | slice 4 review (glm session 5ff7ec63, verified against compile-loop/clojure.cljc:879-955 and ast_walker.cljc zero :tail? references) | yang.clojure | slice 5 (all three: one pre-pass rides the outcome-channel work) | P3 |\n| test-strategy: the test:routed docs gate checks working-tree-vs-index only, so a fully-staged or untracked docs change verifies zero bytes and reports green; closing route: diff against HEAD and print \"unchecked (untracked)\" for paths absent from ls-files; regression probes to follow (TS-P3-01) | test-strategy review (glm session af452dd9, verified against affected.clj:648-656 changed-file sources) | dev.tooling | test-strategy-feedback-contract (QA/codex) | P3 |\n| test-strategy: exit 0 conflates green-gate with JVM-feedback-only for :foundation dispatch, and an empty shard map passes vacuously (every? on [] is true); an automation wrapper cannot distinguish feedback-only fr