he vocabulary assertion; track upstream namespace-metadata issue (not posted); JVM continues to inspect namespace and var docs | P3 |\n75:| Closed 2026-10-23: yin.demo failed on JVM and jolt at the first transfer when a closure-bearing store crossed VMs with different task secrets (`:foreign-value`, `:closure`); pre-existing on master since 6b8502fd | J3 follow-up; owner authorized the separate demo fix | demo owner | one shared capability secret for two execution sites of one logical task; `bb demo` and `bb demo:jolt` pass, G3 green | closed |\n110:| Mixed lock families: a Node session holding a store directory via its `lock.<pid>.<nonce>` claim file and an OS-lock host (jolt — from J4b — JVM, Dart) holding via fcntl are invisible to each other; simultaneous use of one store directory across the two families can double-own and corrupt. Sequential reopen is unaffected and tested. Pre-existing between JVM and Node; jolt inherits it, does not create it. JVM/Dart/jolt mutual exclusion via fcntl IS enforced and gated. | J4 design §3 cross-host limit; fable J4 review F5; owner ruling 2026-10-25 \"document it\" (option a of the three-way: record, best-effort refusal, or common-lock design) | jolt lane (J4b) | documented limitation — the ledger row is the fix. A future common-lock design (option c) would supersede; the best-effort Node-claim refusal (option b) remains available as an enhancement if the accident ever occurs in practice. J4b's acceptance must not claim universal cross-runtime exclusion | P2 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
