da3 and pushed. This unblocks CIC plan Phases 1-3 typing implementation. (2) Slice 4 (sonnet #2, yang-s4 worktree) DELIVERED per fable's design: loop/recur worker lowering, recur-target tracking, Z-combinators deleted, function-level + multi-arity recur, depth gates (walker+semantic 0/100/1000 constant-depth), oracle fixtures, 2 ledger-assigned rejections. Disclosed deviations: walker negative control impossible (walker masks missing flags — architect's own fact; semantic negative control implemented and passing); mk-fresh case->if rewrite pending slice 6 case; extra scaffold primitives. Local verification: focused 90/942 green, kondo 0 errors/5 pre-existing; quick tier IN FLIGHT. (3) Kimi: THREE dispatch attempts failed — (a) agent-file+session mutually exclusive (CLI error; reference now known to under-document this), (b,c) session exits after planning with thinking-only stream error (provider.api_error). Root cause hypothesis: headless -p cannot pass plan-approval pauses; --auto cannot combine with -p (CLI error). Diagnosis logged for the reference; will retry with a fresh session without plan friction, or route to glm as the reviewer bench alternative.\n91:Done: After my three failed kimi dispatches, the owner pointed me back to delegate-invocation-reference.md; re-reading showed my deviations: --output-format text (recipe: stream-json), agent-file+session combination (reference: bind at creation, never on resume), -m on --resume (wrong), --auto with -p (forbidden), and a wrong root-cause hypothesis (the \"early exits\" were likely text-mode stream misreads). Re-dispatched EXACTLY per the canonical recipe (fresh session, stream-json): SUCCESS — 38 tool events, full five-section report (12KB, collab/1793214000000-kimi-test-strategy-investigation-r2.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md), session session_b1a13f11-3550-4a81-9a33-ce657a538a31 (captured from ~/.kimi-code/session_index.jsonl). Findings highlight: the selection mechanism is NOT the bottleneck (test:changed:list on yang.clojure.cljc = 1.26s, 61/327 namespaces) — EXECUTION is (unsharded JVM changed lane timed out at 300s); cold prerequisites regenerate ANTLR 3x; wide-change exit-2 is not fail-closed as a workflow. Recommendations: (policy) explicit change-class->gate routing table incl. automatic G3 on wide changes; (mechanics) make SHARDED quick verification the default G2/G3 path (4-6 JVM workers on laptop, remote for lanes predicted >15min, content-keyed artifact caching, warm worktree pool); (structure) retime before re-tiering, medium tier, split mega-suites by contract. Highest-leverage: sharded-by-default G2/G3 execution with automatic wide-change dispatch. Full measured baselines incl. history mining from the old orchestrator log per owner instruction.\n289:Done: Slice 8 (immutable latte kernel context threading) delivered by codex (440d5fd1 pre-rebase); rebased onto moved master as f7250f03; locally verified 137/2155 + kondo clean. glm adversarial review (session 17a1aad0): APPROVE — all six deliverables verified against pinned upstream, deviations plan-conformant, 4 P3 polish items none blocking (findings synced to main collab). Astra sign-off attempt hit its usage limit (resets 21:11); per the recorded widened-bench ruling, the architect sign-off taken from glm on its own review (session 17a1aad0 resumed): SIGN-OFF GRANTED for f7250f03, condition = shiva Node/Dart lanes green at the exact merged tree. Force-with-lease push (origin had the engineer's pre-rebase push at 440d5fd1 — pushed despite the brief; noted), shiva clones re-pointed, lanes relaunched.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
